From 467b10c13b82482f0db1be40a34f3221f2766141 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 23:40:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/9] FK-16 (0.3.32 candidate): explicit agentCallers opt-in;
 release prerequisites gate

- Default unchanged from 0.3.31: agent callers decide only as themselves; without per-agent
  delegation installed they are refused (unavailable), and the refusal names the opt-in.
- authority.local.agentCallers: "per-agent" (default) | "executor-grants", validated in feltkit().
  executor-grants: an agent caller naming no agent is decided as the executor with its grants
  (wider authority, as through 0.3.30), only while per-agent delegation is absent; marked
  compatibility: "executor-grants" on the decision and activity record; readiness warns
  (authority.agent-callers). Named-agent decisions never fall back. No effect when per-agent
  delegation is installed.
- test/authority-compat.test.ts: never skipped; asserts whichever contract is installed.
- scripts/release-prerequisites.mjs (from release-check): capability probes for @authboundry/local,
  @appport/services and @feltdb/core; installed files compared with the registry tarball;
  fails on skipped compatibility tests or an artifact without the correction.
- Docs and CHANGELOG: rationale, migration, compatibility matrix; 0.3.31's unmet prerequisites.
