diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index 6b87486..a08e40b 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -1,25 +1,43 @@
 # Changelog
 
-## 0.3.32 (release candidate, unpublished): FK-16 authority compatibility
+## 0.3.32 (release candidate, unpublished): FK-16 release integrity and explicit agent-caller compatibility
 
 0.3.31 was published while the per-agent delegation it uses needed an `@authboundry/local` release that does not
-exist (the only published one is 0.1.0, without `registerAgent`). With 0.1.0, every decision by an agent caller was
-`unavailable`, breaking applications whose agents relied on their executor's grants (supported through 0.3.30).
-
-- **Compatibility, not a new model.** With an `@authboundry/local` that has no `registerAgent`, no grant can name an
-  agent (such grants are refused), so only executor grants exist. An agent caller that names no agent is decided as
-  the executor, with its grants, exactly as through 0.3.30 (and as with a hosted AuthBoundry). The decision carries
-  `compatibility: "executor-grants"` and so does its activity record; the first such decision is logged.
-- **Unchanged and still refused:** a decision that names an agent (`agent: "x"`) is `unavailable` (it asked for
-  per-agent authority); an agent naming another agent is a deny; grants naming an agent and `ctx.authority.agents`
-  are `FAILED_PRECONDITION`. Nothing becomes an allow that was not one through 0.3.30.
-- **With an `@authboundry/local` that has per-agent delegation**, 0.3.31's behaviour applies unchanged: an agent
-  caller decides as itself and the executor's grants never apply to it. Moving to that model changes who has
-  authority for existing applications (owners must grant each agent); it will ship in a minor release with
-  migration guidance, not in a patch.
+exist (the only published one is 0.1.0, without `registerAgent`). With 0.1.0 every decision by an agent caller is
+`unavailable`; applications whose agents relied on their executor's grants (the model through 0.3.30) stopped
+working. 0.3.32 keeps 0.3.31's security posture and makes the old behaviour an explicit owner decision.
+
+- **Default unchanged (fail closed).** An agent caller decides only as itself. Without per-agent delegation installed
+  it is refused (`unavailable`), and the refusal now names the opt-in below. People's and services' decisions are
+  unaffected.
+- **New: `authority.local: { agentCallers: "executor-grants" }`.** An application owner may choose, while per-agent
+  delegation is not installed, to let an agent caller that names no agent be decided as the executor with the
+  executor's grants, as through 0.3.30. **This widens authority**: every agent can do whatever people granted the
+  executor. It is not equivalent in security to per-agent delegation. Such decisions carry
+  `compatibility: "executor-grants"` (decision and activity record), the first is logged, and readiness shows a
+  warning (`authority.agent-callers`). Validated when the app is defined: `"per-agent"` (default) or
+  `"executor-grants"`.
+- **Never widened:** a decision that names an agent is `unavailable` (no fallback); an agent naming another agent is a
+  deny; grants naming an agent and `ctx.authority.agents` stay `FAILED_PRECONDITION` without per-agent delegation.
+  With per-agent delegation installed, `agentCallers` has no effect: agents decide as themselves.
+- **Readiness:** `authority.agent-callers` reports the effective mode: `per-agent` (pass), `refused` (warn),
+  `executor-grants` (warn: agents share the executor's grants).
+- **Migrating from 0.3.30:** to keep agents working on `@authboundry/local` 0.1.0, add
+  `agentCallers: "executor-grants"` deliberately. To leave it: install an `@authboundry/local` with per-agent
+  delegation, register agents (`ctx.authority.agents.register`, an operator's act; `app.agent`s register at start),
+  have people grant each agent (`grants.grant({ agent })`), then remove `agentCallers`.
 - **Release integrity.** `test/authority-compat.test.ts` covers agent callers against the installed
-  `@authboundry/local` and never skips; `scripts/release-check.mjs` fails when the authority tests skip a
-  compatibility case or the packed artifact lacks this correction.
+  `@authboundry/local`, never skips, and fails when it is not installed; `scripts/release-check.mjs` verifies the
+  release prerequisites by capability (not version), refuses skipped compatibility tests, and checks that the packed
+  artifact contains this change.
+
+### Compatibility matrix
+
+| `@authboundry/local` installed | `agentCallers` | Agent caller, no `agent` named | Decision naming an agent |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| without `registerAgent` (0.1.0, the only published) | unset / `"per-agent"` | `unavailable` | `unavailable` |
+| without `registerAgent` | `"executor-grants"` | executor's grants, marked `compatibility` | `unavailable` |
+| with per-agent delegation (unreleased) | any | as itself, with only grants to it | as that registered agent |
 
 ## Unreleased (content released as 0.3.31; prerequisites below were NOT met at that release)
 
